## 17. Limitations

The current implementation is primarily designed as an academic/prototype system.

Some limitations include:

* Large-scale real-world networks may require more advanced optimization.
* Community quality depends on the selected detection method.
* Real social networks may contain noisy or incomplete data.
* Dynamic changes in social networks are not fully modeled.
* Visualization becomes difficult for extremely large graphs.

